# Testing

Every behavior-changing task must include the tests named in its sprint spec. Documentation-only tasks need a file and consistency review, not runtime tests.

Prefer tests at domain and application boundaries over brittle UI snapshots.

- Phase 1: unit-test domain, use cases, and mock/static repositories. UI may depend on use cases, not JSON fixtures.
- Phase 2: API tests and repository tests per Sprint 5 tooling.
- Do not hit real payment/email providers in CI; use fakes.
- Do not merge a task whose stated tests fail.
- Do not skip tests to bypass architecture (e.g. testing a page that reads fixtures directly).

After implementation: run the checks listed in the task (lint/test/build as they exist). If tooling is not initialized yet (before S1-T03/S1-T06), do not install it unless that is the current task.
